<p>In 1982, Rob Thomson and William Palmer set out to convert the <em>Oxford Book of English Verse</em> into &#8220;non-emotive, non-sexist, modern language.&#8221; They began with the opening lines of Wordsworth&#8217;s &#8220;The Solitary Reaper&#8221;:</p>
<p>Behold her, single in the field,<br />
Yon solitary Highland Lass!<br />
Reaping and singing by herself;<br />
Stop here, or gently pass!</p>
<p><a href="https://archive.org/details/lastcuckooverybe0000unse/page/82/mode/2up">The new version</a>:</p>
<p>Look at solo Ms McPherson,<br />
In her field, a single person,<br />
Cutting corn with vocal tune,<br />
Stop, or leave her all alone.</p>
<p>There&#8217;s no sign they got any further.</p>
